# Applications the Omarchy menu offers that have no aarch64 build.
#
# Format: <package name> <reason>
#
# Separate from packages.unavailable, which is about install/omarchy-base.packages
# and is read by the installer. This file is about the apps a user installs
# afterwards, from the menu or from `omarchy pkg add`, and it is read at runtime
# by omarchy-pkg-arm-source.
#
# It exists because on x86_64 most of these come from the [omarchy] repository,
# which has no aarch64 tree. Without this list the only thing pacman can say on
# ARM is "target not found", which reads like a broken install rather than an
# application that was never built for the machine.
#
# Every line was checked against the Arch Linux ARM databases and, where the
# package exists in the AUR, against the arch=() line of its PKGBUILD.

1password                     proprietary, the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
dropbox                       proprietary, the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
nautilus-dropbox              the AUR package builds for x86_64 only, and dropbox itself has no ARM build
google-chrome                 proprietary, the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
microsoft-edge-stable-bin     proprietary, the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
spotify                       proprietary, the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
zed                           the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
symfony-cli                   the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
heroic-games-launcher-bin     the AUR package builds for x86_64 only

# The Windows compatibility stack is x86 by construction: Arch Linux ARM ships
# no wine at all, and Steam lives in [multilib], which does not exist here.
steam                         [multilib] does not exist on aarch64
wine-staging                  the AUR package builds for x86_64 and i686 only
wine-mono                     not built for aarch64 by Arch Linux ARM
wine-gecko                    not built for aarch64 by Arch Linux ARM
umu-launcher                  the AUR package builds for x86_64 only
